      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxide film forms on the alloy surface during high-temperature wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film is protective against corrosion before it is mechanically disrupted.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical wear repeatedly ruptures the surface oxide film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rupture of the oxide film exposes fresh surfaces of both the FCC and σ phases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The potential difference between the FCC and σ phases establishes galvanic cells.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Galvanic coupling produces localized corrosion at FCC/σ interfaces.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Corrosion-induced structural weakening makes the alloy more susceptible to subsequent wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mutual acceleration of corrosion and wear creates a positive feedback loop that accelerates total degradation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under simultaneous elevated-temperature wear and corrosion, the multiphase eutectic HEA will have greater total degradation than a matched single-phase FCC HEA.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The multiphase eutectic HEA will have a higher corrosion current density than the single-phase baseline.",
